Package: R_comparison_digitalization_method
Title: Compare variability between two digitizing methods
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Felix", "Guillaud", , "guillaudfelix@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: After extracting coordinates of fish body midlines using MATLAb and ImageJ method (see report), coordinates are used to calculate inter-operator, inter-method, and intra-operator variability. Finally both methods are replicable and reapetable with low variability due to the operator or the method. We choose the MATLAB method for further analysis because it was smoother and already published.
